012 Olympic Games, where he was fifth. They knew each other well having previously fought five times before. Midway through the first period of their gold medal match, Vlasov scored four points, and picked up another point in the next period after Madsen’s corner unsuccessfully challenged a call. And after giving up a point for passivity late in the match, Vlasov took a 5-1 victory  over Madsen, winning his second Olympic gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the semi-finals, Vlasov was in the lead when he was choked unconscious by " [:a {:href "/athletes/133341"} "Božo Starčević"] " of Croatia on a legal move, and while officials awarded Starčević two points, they stopped the bout when they realized Vlasov had blacked out. Madsen beat Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117179"} "Péter Bácsi"] ", competing in his third Olympics, in the other semi-final, sending Starčević and Bácsi to the bronze medal matches. There, the 2014 World champion Bácsi lost to 2011 World champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/122823"} "Saeid Abdevali"] " of Iran, while Starčević lost to Kim."] "\n\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/120372"} "Roman Vlasov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/R